# Working on {{.Name}}

Read README.md first. Run pluto fmt and pluto vet before submitting changes.
Keep every file <=1,000 lines; prefer expanded readable Go and 80 columns.

pluto.toml schema 6 owns endpoint/feature/capability metadata. *_gen.go is CLI-owned.
Handlers, models, operations, composition root and transport helpers are authored
and created once. Never add magic init registration. Add endpoints with the CLI.
Do not import HTTP/storage from operations or database adapters from handlers,
even indirectly. Define narrow interfaces in consumers; inject constructors.

HTTP primitives are app-local. Authorization uses the pinned published
pluto-rbac module. Authored access.Roles starts empty; adding endpoints must never
grant roles automatically. Keep one compiled policy injected into route and
operation checks through Dependencies.Policy. Resolve Principal.Roles from trusted
membership; unknown roles and nil policies must deny capability checks.
Use the published Pluto session manager and HTTP adapter; preserve exact Origin
checks for cookie writes and reject ambiguous credentials. Supply a trusted credential provider;
verify membership before creating a tenant principal. Preserve verified tenant
scope in every domain-specific repository. Permissions do not prove resource
ownership; flags never grant authorization. Never log bodies, tokens or secrets.

OpenAPI derives from paths and concrete models. Regenerate with
`go run ./cmd/openapi`; pluto vet verifies freshness. Use native fuzz tests and
operation/HTTP behavior tests. PostgreSQL connectivity is optional; generated
operations explicitly return not implemented and do not persist data.

Per-endpoint `internal/app/<group>_<action>.go` bindings are authored constructor
choices. Change the operation constructor and this binding together when adding
repositories. Add typed fields to app.Dependencies and construct/inject them in
app.New. Generated group registries accept narrow Operations interfaces and never
choose concrete implementations; additions preserve authored constructor wiring.

Local-password apps use password.Service with postgres.NewLocal for both accounts
and sessions. Never use direct Manager.Start/session-only issuance for local
accounts. Keep delivery, shared account limits and trusted client/concurrency
Ingress explicit; missing integrations fail startup. Auth responses never enter
idempotency capture. Enrollment never grants membership or roles. No startup DDL.

Jobs use the published Pluto Jobs runtime. EnqueueTx shares the exact business
transaction; never silently split enqueue and commit. Handlers validate tenant
ownership, honor cancellation and make effects idempotent. No auth challenge,
password, cookie or token belongs in durable job payloads. Preserve authored job
handlers and CLI-owned explicit registration. Run cmd/worker separately; no
startup DDL or implicit goroutines. Empty/unimplemented workers must not fake
successful delivery. Apply 005_jobs.sql explicitly to existing databases.
